---
description: Delegate a long coding job in this repo to the local Forge agent through the file mailbox
alwaysApply: false
---

Use the Forge file bridge when a task should run as a real Forge chat (multi-file edits, a long local-agent loop) and VS Code is open with `forge.bridge.enabled` turned on. Do small edits yourself.

Send work with `_devtools/bridge/forge-bridge ask "<subject>" "<task>"` (optional `--session`, `--mode`, `--timeout`). Or `bridge send cursor forge "<subject>" "<task>"` and read the reply with `bridge read cursor`.

How it works, the `@session` / `@mode` lines, and the limits are in `docs/CURSOR_BRIDGE.md`.
